<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        ADDED 2026-08-25 (native LOI/PSA Details). Sibling of Primary_LOI__c in this folder -
        read that file first; everything it says about why the lookup exists, the retracted
        "there is no Primary_LOI__c/Primary_PSA__c" claim, the stamp being load-bearing, and
        the FLS divergence from Primary_NDA__c applies here unchanged. THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE
        THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY.

        🔴 THE NAME IS `Primary_PSA__c`, NOT `Primary_Contract__c`, AND THAT IS A DELIBERATE
        BREAK FROM THE OPPORTUNITY TWIN (Opportunity.Primary_Contract__c). The disposition side
        of this application calls this stage PSA everywhere a user can see it -
        Disposition_Stage__c's value is 'PSA', the record type is Disposition_PSA, and this
        object already carries PSA_Executed__c. `Primary_PSA__c` is the name the nine formula
        fields' PSA_* prefix and the FlexiPage section both read from.

        ⚠ IT DOES NOT COLLIDE SEMANTICALLY WITH THE EXISTING PSA_Executed__c, AND THE TWO WERE
        COMPARED BEFORE THIS NAME WAS CHOSEN. PSA_Executed__c is a plain CHECKBOX on the
        disposition itself, set on the disposition's own record - it is the disposition's
        assertion that a PSA is done. Primary_PSA__c is a LOOKUP to the Contract_Review__c row,
        and PSA_Execution_Date__c (this change) is a FORMULA reading that row's own
        Execution_Date__c. So: PSA_Executed__c = what this disposition says, Primary_PSA__c /
        PSA_Execution_Date__c = what the contract record says. They can legitimately disagree,
        and nothing in this change synchronises them - deliberately, because inventing that
        rule was not asked for and would silently overwrite whichever side a user edited last.

        referenceTo is Contract_Review__c (the object behind the "PSA" label in this module);
        relationshipName is PrimaryDispositions, unique on that object beside PrimaryOpportunities
        (Opportunity.Primary_Contract__c) and Contract_Reviews (Contract_Review__c.Disposition__c).
    -->
    <fullName>Primary_PSA__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>The primary PSA / Contract Review for this disposition - stamped by the PSA stage-entry automation and spanned by the PSA_*__c formula fields that the PSA-stage Details section renders.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Set automatically when the disposition Contract Review is created. It points the PSA Details section at the right record, so it is not maintained by hand.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Primary PSA</label>
    <referenceTo>Contract_Review__c</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Dispositions (Primary PSA)</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>PrimaryDispositions</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackFeedHistory>false</trackFeedHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
